Package: emeans
Title: Fast Unsupervised Subtyping of Expression Data with e-means
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Dingkang", "Zhao", email = "dingkang.25@intl.zju.edu.cn",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Unsupervised molecular subtyping of bulk expression matrices.
    Samples are clustered with e-means, a k-means variant whose centroids
    follow an exponentially decaying average with a cosine-annealed step size
    and periodic revival of under-used centroids. One call takes a
    genes-by-samples matrix, imputes missing values with gene medians, drops
    constant genes, standardises each gene, reduces the matrix to principal
    components and clusters the samples, returning subtype labels, subtype
    centroids on the input scale, silhouette diagnostics, the scan over
    candidate numbers of subtypes, marker genes and a predictor for new
    samples. The clustering engine is exported as well, for matrices that are
    already samples by features. The method is described in Bessa, Mazare,
    Szilvasy, Touvron, Picard, Douze and Jegou (2026)
    <https://e-means.github.io>.
